{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":6556775,"ns":0,"title":"Ecstasy (philosophy)","extract":"In existential philosophy, ecstasy (from the Ancient Greek ἔκστασις [ékstasis] 'to be or stand outside oneself, a removal to elsewhere'; from ek- 'out' and stasis 'stand' or 'standoff of forces') describes a sense of being \"outside-itself\". One's consciousness, for example, is not self-enclosed, as one can be conscious of an Other person, who falls well outside one's own self.","description":"Term used in philosophy with different meanings in different traditions","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}